+Krylov-based solvers directly and remove the cost of assembly altogether. Their scope is
+different from ours. Interior-point solvers such as \texttt{Clarabel} and \texttt{MOSEK},
+and operator-splitting solvers such as \texttt{SCS} and \texttt{OSQP} in their default
+direct mode, factorize a matrix built from $\mmat{A}$ and $\mmat{P}$, and therefore need
+these matrices explicitly. This thesis
